      "content": "The permanence you feel is a heavy blanket, but it's also a very convincing illusion that can be lifted. When everything feels like a void, it's often because the pain has become so vast it obscures any possibility of change. A therapist can help you find the small cracks in that void, showing you that even when things feel permanent, your capacity for feeling and change remains.",
